o WorkflowError-from-LLMUnavailableError site","dbca test test_execute_base_and_outage_still_llm_unavailable and 35ab test assert on a synthetic bare `WorkflowError('execute step failed: provider overloaded')` — a fixture string, not a production propagation path"],"finding":"The cause/context-walking WorkflowError->llm_unavailable branch (Operator decision + AC1) targets an exception shape with no production producer. Execute-step LLM failures are caught at interpreter.py:510 (`except Exception`) and converted to in-band StepResult(status='failed'), never re-raised; the only production `raise WorkflowError` is editor.py:475 (missing-bundle, no cause). No production site raises a `WorkflowError` from an `LLMUnavailableError` cause/context.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1b9d993bee0d66ab","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Operator decision para 2 ('a compatibility wrapper WorkflowError raised from a real LLMUnavailableError cause/context also maps to llm_unavailable') and AC1","norm_id":"nc90f881187ae7b7e","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds __cause__/__context__ traversal to error_code_for and focused 'both execute-outage paths' tests, but the tests can only exercise hand-constructed Workflow(...) from LLMUnavailableError() fixtures that no production code emits — pinning dead behavior"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Since a genuine LLMUnavailableError propagates as itself and is already caught by the narrowed branch 7, and the plan's own intent routes bare WorkflowError to command_failed, remove the cause/context traversal entirely. Reframe AC1 to require only: direct LLMUnavailableError->llm_unavailable, and (if kept) document that the dbca AC3 'execute step failed' fixture now correctly maps to command_failed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the premise about execute-step outage propagation: state where an LLMUnavailableError is actually observable as an exception reaching error_code_for (e.g. _structured_llm_failure / _mcp_llm surface, not run_workflow's swallowed step path), and scope the preservation test to that real seam.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["interpreter.py:490-511: the `with usage_log.step_identity(...): result = _dispatch(...)` call is wrapped in `except Exception as exc: result = StepResult(outputs={}, status='failed', error=str(exc))` — the exception is captured as data, not propagated","interpreter.py raise-sites are only ExpressionError (input resolution) and a re-raise at line 624; no LLMUnavailableError re-raise out of run_workflow"],"finding":"The plan asserts as an established premise that 'Production execute-step outages already propagate as LLMUnavailableError', which the code does not support: at interpreter.py:510 any step exception (including an LLMUnavailableError) is swallowed into a failed StepResult and run_workflow returns normally, so error_code_for is never handed an execute-step outage exception from that surface.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8cbdbcce63f042b5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Operator decision para 2 ('Production execute-step outages already propagate as LLMUnavailableError') and AC1 ('production execute-step outages propagated as LLMUnavailableError')","norm_id":"nc406f57e69947e70","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes a 'production execute-step outage' focused test expecting error_code_for to receive an LLMUnavailableError from the run surface, but run_workflow never raises it"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the WorkflowError-outage cause/context walk decision rule: state the walk is arbitrary-depth over both __cause__ and __context__ (cause preferred), cycle-safe (reuse the structured_run.py:302 / failure.py helper), and state explicitly whether it keys on the bare WorkflowError type only or on all non-caller WorkflowError subclasses (fixing SnapshotError's llm_unavailable-vs-command_failed treatment).","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a compatibility wrapper WorkflowError raised from a real LLMUnavailableError cause/context also maps to llm_unavailable'","AC1: 'for WorkflowError cause/context chains containing LLMUnavailableError'","Current error_code_for (_errors.py:131-219) performs NO __cause__/__context__ walk in any branch — the compatibility mapping is new behavior the plan does not fully pin","Repo already has a canonical arbitrary-depth, cause-over-context, cycle-safe walk at src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:302-310 and src/rebar/llm/failure.py:464 that the plan could name to remove the ambiguity","SnapshotError(WorkflowError) at snapshot.py:83 is a WorkflowError subclass NOT in _workflow_caller_code and NOT in the availability subtree; the plan scopes the outage rule to 'plain/bare WorkflowError' yet the cause-walk phrasing leaves its treatment (llm_unavailable vs command_failed) ambiguous"],"finding":"The WorkflowError-outage-compatibility rule ('a compatibility wrapper WorkflowError raised from a real LLMUnavailableError cause/context also maps to llm_unavailable'; AC1: 'WorkflowError cause/context chains containing LLMUnavailableError') under-specifies the chain-walk decision rule the executor branch must implement: depth (single hop vs arbitrary), __cause__-vs-__context__ precedence, cycle-safety, and whether the walk keys on the BARE WorkflowError type only or on ALL non-caller WorkflowError subclasses (e.g. SnapshotError from snapshot.py:83 carrying an outage cause).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f194e7bed6447a5c0","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Operator decision' / 'Intended mapping' / AC1; src/rebar/_errors.py branch 6-7; src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py","norm_id":"n120e6db3d85ffe96","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A workflow execute step catches an LLMUnavailableError and re-raises a compatibility WorkflowError chained only via __context__ (not __cause__) -> misclassified as command_failed if the walk only follows __cause__","An outage wrapped two hops deep in the chain -> misclassified if the walk is single-hop","A SnapshotError raised over an LLMUnavailableError cause -> undefined whether it is an outage or command_failed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify: walk exc's __cause__/__context__ chain to arbitrary depth (cause preferred, cycle-safe) using the existing structured_run helper; if any node is an LLMUnavailableError -> llm_unavailable; apply this to any WorkflowError that is not already classified by an earlier branch (so SnapshotError with an outage cause is llm_unavailable, otherwise command_failed), and add a focused test for the __context__-only and depth>1 cases.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"check